implementationPlan.description:
Tests first (DoD 1, 2), in scripts/tests/postflight-worktree.cjs. Read mem:gotcha-postflight-worktree-git-stub before touching the stub.

(a) Add two knobs to both the sh `git` stub and `git.ps1` (stub() ~:120-175). Document them in the stub's header comment.
- WT_GIT_PUSH_REMOTE_REJECTED=1: a `push` call whose argv holds `--porcelain` runs the REAL push with its output discarded, so origin really holds C. It then prints `To <remote>`, `!<TAB><last argv><TAB>[remote rejected] (wt stub: applied, then refused)` and `Done`, and exits 1.
- WT_GIT_FETCH_FAIL_AFTER_PUSH=<marker file>: that push also creates the marker. While the marker exists, every `fetch` fails (exit 1), so all 3 land_fetch tries of the re-check fail. L4's fetch before the push is untouched.
- In git.ps1, print the porcelain lines on the success stream and fail with `Write-Error` plus exit 1 (the gotcha). In the sh argv scan, use distinct flag letters.

(b) Add a new case 'wt-remote-rejected' and register it in `cases`. Use a bare origin (as wtUnlanded's bare() helper does) and a REVIEW landing (landRun with REVIEW and MOE_LAND_NET_BACKOFF_SEC 0). Two arms:
- applied, with WT_GIT_PUSH_REMOTE_REJECTED=1. Assert:
  - origin's main is the landed C;
  - finals(p) is [['landed', C]];
  - the last completion row is sha C with pushed:true;
  - there is no refs/moe/rescue/<task>/* ref, and retryOf(p) is null;
  - journal(p) is gone after the run, as after any landed completion (match wtCompletion's assertion);
  - the log has one MOE_PUSH_REMOTE_REJECTED_APPLIED line and no MOE_PUSH_FAILED.
- fetch-fails, the same plus WT_GIT_FETCH_FAIL_AFTER_PUSH. Expect exactly the existing wtUnlanded 'rejected' shape, even though origin holds C, because the DoD keeps that path exactly as before:
  - MOE_PUSH_FAILED;
  - a completion row failed/MOE_PUSH_FAILED/pushed:false;
  - an unlanded finalize with unlandedReason 'remote';
  - a rescue ref at the task-branch tip;
  - landingRetry count 1.

Leave wtUnlanded's 'rejected' arm unchanged (a pre-receive hook, so origin truly refuses): it still proves the not-applied path. The held-out scripts/tests/worktree-landing.{sh,ps1} must pass unchanged; never edit them.

RED at HEAD: the applied arm (MOE_PUSH_FAILED, routed unlanded). The fetch-fails arm is a guard that passes before and after the fix.

Error handling in the harness: give each arm its own repo, bare remote and marker, so no knob leaks into another case. Edit with your TOOL-witnessed editor.

Last: an adversarial self-review of the 5-file diff. Check that:
- a truly refused push (pre-receive hook) still makes exactly ONE push, ends MOE_PUSH_FAILED and moves no tracking ref past B (the held-out remoteRejected case);
- the re-check never re-pushes and never forces;
- a failed or unresolvable fetch is never read as published;
- a C that origin holds only below a peer's later commit still counts (ancestry, not equality);
- the `[rejected]`, unknown and reconcile paths are byte-identical;
- the new line is byte-identical in both wrappers;
- migration landing inherits the re-check correctly;
- no other function and none of the VM-route blocks were touched, and the BOM is intact.

If the review changes any byte, re-run step 4 and submit that fresh output.
